<header><p class="enc-kicker">State</p><h1 class="enc-title">Kanem–Bornu Empire</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Kanem-Bornu, Kanem–Bornu</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-kanem">Kanem</a>–<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bornu">Bornu Empire</a> was a long-lived state around <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lake-chad">Lake Chad</a>, first centred in Kanem and later in Bornu. It was ruled for centuries by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sayfawa-dynasty">Sayfawa dynasty</a> and was among the earliest states in the region to adopt <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/islam">Islam</a>. It has its own profile on the site and reached its height under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/idris-alooma">Idris Alooma</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/kanem-bornu-empire.jpg" alt="Kanem–Bornu Empire" width="320" height="288" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Megartonius · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Kanem%E2%80%93Bornu,_13th_century.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
